# 42. SERVER-SIDE SEO

This is extremely important.

The SEO metadata must actually appear in the HTML delivered to search engines.

Do NOT implement SEO only by changing document.title after the page loads in the browser if the architecture supports proper server-rendered/pre-rendered metadata.

Inspect the existing architecture.

If it is:

* Next.js → use the appropriate Metadata API
* React SPA → determine the best SEO-compatible rendering/prerendering strategy
* Vite/React → do not assume client-only metadata is sufficient for every SEO requirement
* Other framework → use its proper metadata mechanism

Implement according to the actual framework.

